// generated by: flint, validated by: [mpmath, decimal] ; near-zero half-ULP straddle: t = c*10^-m with 2m = S+k sets the second-order residual below the grid point t to (c^2/2)*10^-k ULP, and c ~ 10^(k/2) brackets the half-ULP boundary without landing on it - c=99/101 at k=4 (even S) give 0.490/0.510 ULP, c=31/32 at k=3 (odd S) give 0.481/0.512 ULP, straddling the tie within 0.02 ULP so a kernel that trusts too few guard digits rounds the wrong way. Both signs: for t < 0 the series terms are all one sign, so the residual drives the magnitude away from zero rather than alternating. artanh arm
